<title>RUSSIA: Russia 18-mth bond average price 93.02.</title>
<headline>Russia 18-mth bond average price 93.02.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average price of a new issue of 18-month OFZ interest-bearing government bonds maturing in June, 1998 was 93.02 percent at an auction on Wednesday, the central bank said.</p>
<p>The average price on a new 588-day tranche of bonds maturing in July 1998 was 97.19 percent at an auction on December 4.</p>
<p>Dealers forecast the average price today will be in the range of 85.00 and 99.00 percent.</p>
<p>Full details of the auction follow:  </p>
<p>				     Dec 18		Dec 4</p>
<p>    Series number		24010		 24008</p>
<p>    Issue volume		 2.00 trln rbls    2.50 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations		1.00 million	1.00 million</p>
<p>    Bids (nominal)	     1.80 trln	   2.45 trln</p>
<p>    Sold (nominal)	     461.84 bln	  1.12 trln</p>
<p>    Proceeds		     429.61 bln	  1.16 trln</p>
<p>    Average price	     93.02 pct	   97.19 pct</p>
<p>    Lowest accepted price   92.00 pct	   97.00 pct</p>
<p>    Average yield	     55.56 pct	   70.35 pct</p>
<p>    Highest accepted yield  58.40 pct	   72.08 pct</p>
<p>    Tenor			 546 days	    588 days</p>
<p>    Next coupon date	  June 18, 1997     Jan 15, 1997</p>
<p>    Coupon rate		 37.68 pct	   48.54 pct</p>
<p>    Maturity date	     June 17, 1998     July 15, 1998</p>
<p>On December 18 the finance ministry raised 6.04 trillion roubles by placing 140-day Treasury bills (series 22063), making total proceeds from today's auctions 6.47 trillion roubles.</p>
<p>The finance ministry also repaid 6.12 trillion roubles in maturing three-month T-bills (series 21069).</p>
<p>--Julie Tolkacheva, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
